WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.726
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Long Breath Out.

00:00:14.726 --> 00:00:21.451
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:21.451 --> 00:00:25.486
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:29.522
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:38.937
This is a breathing practice with a simple shape. The breath in is small and gentle. The breath out is long and slow.

00:00:38.937 --> 00:00:49.698
We will count it like this: breathe in — two, three. Then let the air leak out — two, three, four, five. Longer out than in.

00:00:49.698 --> 00:01:01.804
The out-breath is a leak, not a push. Like air slipping out of a balloon, slowly. Or blowing a dandelion so softly that the seeds stay right where they are.

00:01:01.804 --> 00:01:07.185
Nothing is ever held. The air moves in, the air moves out. That is the whole shape. Here we go.

00:01:07.185 --> 00:01:19.291
Round one. Breathe in… two, three. And let it leak out… two, three, four, five.

00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:31.397
Round two. In… two, three. Out, slow and easy… two, three, four, five.

00:01:31.397 --> 00:01:43.503
Round three. In… two, three. Out… two, three, four, five. Let your shoulders drop a little more with the leak.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:54.264
Round four. In… two, three. Out… two, three, four, five.

00:01:54.264 --> 00:01:55.609
One last round, on your own count. In… and out, as long as feels good. Then let the counting go, and just breathe the way your body wants to.

00:01:55.609 --> 00:02:07.715
Now hear the rules that keep this practice yours. The counts are guides — they are never a test.

00:02:07.715 --> 00:02:19.821
If your out-breath is shorter than five, your practice is still complete. Your breath, your pace. And this is never a contest — not the longest, not the quietest, not the slowest.

00:02:19.821 --> 00:02:29.236
And if anything ever feels dizzy, or tight, or strange, the move is simple: breathe normally. Normal breathing is always allowed, at any second. It is never a failure.

00:02:29.236 --> 00:02:30.581
Notice how your breathing feels now, all on its own. Nothing to fix. Nothing to hold.

00:02:30.581 --> 00:02:39.997
In small. Out long. Then let it be.

00:02:39.997 --> 00:02:46.723
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:46.723 --> 00:02:52.103
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:52.103 --> 00:02:58.829
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:05.554
You're ready for what's next.
